    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here's a potential 2-minute monologue for the first segment of your podcast:\n\n\"You know, there's a phrase they love to throw around: 'experts weigh in.' But what does that even mean? It means the same five people in similar suits are trotting out the same talking points night after night, regardless of the facts. They're not just missing the point, they're actively trying to obscure the truth. It's like they're speaking a language that everyone else in the country doesn't understand.\n\n\"I mean, think about it: have you ever seen a mainstream news anchor ask a senior executive at Starbucks about the real cost of a venti half-caf, half-decaf iced caramel macchiato? No. They don't want to know – they want to pontificate about how the 'carbon molecular structure' of the coffee beans is 'sapping our creativity.' Give me a break.\n\n\"We're taught to trust 'experts' at our peril. They're not gatekeepers of truth; they're gatekeepers of illusions. And the people who surrender control to them – the ones who nod along while the anchors spew scripted platitudes – are the ones who'll get stuck with the credit card bill.\n\n\"The",
